<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa to start non-stop Windhoek flight.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa to start non-stop Windhoek flight.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Lufthansa AG said it will start a twice-weekly non-stop flight to Windhoek, Namibia, from October 28.</p>
<p>The new Mondays and Wednesdays service with a Boeing 747-400 will cut flying time from Germany to Namibia by three hours and 40 minutes to nine and a half hours, a Lufthansa statement said.</p>
<p>Lufthansa previously flew to Windhoek via Johannesburg. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 8982 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
